        <section id="hosting">
          <h2>Hosting Recommendation</h2>
          <p>I recommend <strong>shared hosting</strong>. The site is small and static, traffic is a few hundred visits a day, and shared hosting is the cheapest option with the least administration. A VPS or dedicated server gives 
more control and scalability, but the department does not need it yet.</p>
          <p>The <strong>domain name</strong> gives a readable address, <strong>DNS records</strong> (A record) point the name to the server&rsquo;s IP address, the <strong>hosting server</strong> stores and serves the files, and 
the <strong>control panel</strong> manages files, SSL certificates and email.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="security">
          <h2>Security Considerations</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Use HTTPS so form data is encrypted in transit.</li>
            <li>No passwords or secrets are placed in HTML comments or hidden inputs.</li>
            <li>Browser validation (required, pattern, min/max) helps users, but the server must validate again.</li>
            <li>Future database code must use parameterised queries to prevent SQL injection.</li>
            <li>Uploaded files must be checked for type and size and stored outside the web root.</li>
            <li>Any user input shown back on a page must be escaped to prevent XSS.</li>
            <li>The form collects only the data needed for the visit.</li>
            <li>The hosting account uses a strong password and two-factor authentication.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
